# E2E Required

**All user-facing features must have automated E2E verification** before merge.

## Definition of done (user-facing)

1. Add or extend a spec under `e2e/specs/`.
2. Add stable `data-testid` selectors on new/changed UI.
3. Use **deterministic mocks** when external services are involved (`JARVIS_E2E=1`, `src-tauri/src/e2e.rs`).
4. Run `npm run test:e2e:local` (or CI `e2e` job) green.

## Patterns

| Need | Approach |
|------|----------|
| LLM / embedder | `apply_e2e_config` → Mock providers |
| Feishu / lark-cli | `e2e::lark_fixture_*` + `e2e::lark_auth_status` |
| File index | `JARVIS_E2E_FIXTURE` seeded at startup |
| React inputs | `setReactInputValue` / `clickViaDom` in `e2e/helpers.ts` |

## Spec map

| Area | Spec file |
|------|-----------|
| Full journey | `full-ui.spec.ts` |
| Lark / Feishu | `lark.spec.ts` |
| Memory | `memory.spec.ts` |
| Agent | `agent.spec.ts` |
| Q&A | `qa.spec.ts` |
| Settings / index | `settings.spec.ts` |
| Navigation | `navigation.spec.ts` |
| Smoke | `smoke.spec.ts` |
| Wiki | `wiki.spec.ts` |
| Related-docs | `related-docs.spec.ts` |

New feature → add test to the focused spec **and** extend `full-ui.spec.ts` if it is part of the primary journey.

## CI

Windows job `e2e` runs `npm run test:e2e` (all `e2e/specs/**/*.spec.ts`) on every push to `dev` / `master`.
